 ('p', 'Resizing before compressing multiplies the savings. An image displayed at 800 pixels wide does not need to be 4,000 pixels wide; scaling it down first removes millions of pixels before compression even begins, which is why resizing and compressing together can shrink a file by 95%.'),
 ('h2', 'Common targets and how to hit them'),
